  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_RESPIRATIONINPLANTS_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Structure and function of mitochondrial ATP synthase</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>Study the schematic diagram of ATP synthesis in the inner mitochondrial membrane shown below and identify <strong>X</strong>, <strong>Y</strong>, and the direction of proton movement.</p>
      <div style="margin: 12px 0;">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="460" height="270" viewBox="0 0 460 270">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="460" height="270" fill="#ffffff"/>
          <text x="85" y="30" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Outer side</text>
          <text x="85" y="46" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#555" text-anchor="middle">(Intermembrane space)</text>
          <text x="355" y="30" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Matrix</text>
          <rect x="175" y="25" width="46" height="215" fill="#b3e5fc" stroke="#4fc3f7" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="198" y="255" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Inner mitochondrial membrane</text>
          <rect x="165" y="88" width="66" height="90" rx="14" fill="#ffeb3b" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2"/>
          <rect x="228" y="118" width="38" height="30" fill="#ffeb3b" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2"/>
          <line x1="228" y1="119" x2="228" y2="147" stroke="#ffeb3b" stroke-width="4"/>
          <circle cx="305" cy="133" r="44" fill="#ffeb3b" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2"/>
          <line x1="264" y1="120" x2="264" y2="146" stroke="#ffeb3b" stroke-width="4"/>
          <text x="198" y="122" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#111" text-anchor="middle">X</text>
          <text x="305" y="122" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#111" text-anchor="middle">Y</text>
          <line x1="85" y1="133" x2="365" y2="133" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/>
          <polygon points="365,133 355,128 355,138" fill="#111"/>
          <text x="115" y="123" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#111" text-anchor="middle">2H⁺</text>
          <line x1="305" y1="205" x2="305" y2="62" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/>
          <polygon points="305,62 300,72 310,72" fill="#111"/>
          <text x="305" y="55" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#111" text-anchor="middle">ATP</text>
          <line x1="278" y1="225" x2="305" y2="195" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <line x1="332" y1="225" x2="305" y2="195" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <text x="272" y="238" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#111" text-anchor="middle">ADP</text>
          <text x="338" y="238" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#111" text-anchor="middle">Pi</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p>Which of the following correctly describes <strong>X</strong> and <strong>Y</strong>?</p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The diagram depicts ATP synthase (Complex V) situated across the inner mitochondrial membrane. Component <strong>X</strong> is embedded within the lipid bilayer, component <strong>Y</strong> protrudes into the mitochondrial matrix, \(2\text{H}^+\) ions move across <strong>X</strong> from the outer side (intermembrane space) toward the matrix, and \(\text{ADP} + \text{P}_\text{i}\) are converted to \(\text{ATP}\) at <strong>Y</strong>.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Sign Conventions</strong><br/>An electrochemical proton gradient is established across the inner mitochondrial membrane with a higher proton concentration on the outer side (intermembrane space) than in the matrix.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>According to the chemiosmotic hypothesis, Complex V (ATP synthase) consists of two major components: \(F_0\) and \(F_1\). The \(F_0\) component is an integral membrane protein complex forming the proton channel, while the \(F_1\) headpiece is a peripheral membrane protein complex facing the matrix that contains the catalytic site for ATP synthesis.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>1. Since <strong>X</strong> spans the inner mitochondrial membrane and forms the channel through which \(2\text{H}^+\) pass per ATP synthesised, <strong>X</strong> represents \(F_0\).<br/>2. Since <strong>Y</strong> is a globular headpiece projecting into the matrix where \(\text{ADP} + \text{P}_\text{i} \rightarrow \text{ATP}\) occurs, <strong>Y</strong> represents \(F_1\).<br/>3. Protons move down their electrochemical gradient from the intermembrane space to the mitochondrial matrix through \(F_0\).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>The structure and proton flow match the chemiosmotic mechanism of oxidative phosphorylation. Therefore, <strong>X</strong> is \(F_0\) (integral membrane protein channel) and <strong>Y</strong> is \(F_1\) (peripheral membrane protein complex containing the catalytic site for ATP synthesis in the matrix).</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>X</strong> is \(F_0\) (integral membrane protein channel) and <strong>Y</strong> is \(F_1\) (peripheral membrane protein complex with the catalytic site for ATP synthesis).</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>X</strong> is \(F_1\) (integral membrane protein channel) and <strong>Y</strong> is \(F_0\) (peripheral membrane protein complex with the catalytic site for ATP synthesis).</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>X</strong> is \(F_0\) (peripheral membrane protein complex) and <strong>Y</strong> is \(F_1\) (integral membrane protein channel pumping protons into the intermembrane space).</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>X</strong> is cytochrome \(c\) (mobile electron carrier) and <strong>Y</strong> is \(F_1\) (catalytic site for NADH oxidation).</p>]]></text></answer>
