  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_RESPIRATIONINPLANTS_DIAGRAM_Q02 - Major pathways of anaerobic respiration</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>The diagram below illustrates the major pathways of anaerobic respiration starting from glucose. Identify the labels <strong>P</strong>, <strong>Q</strong>, <strong>R</strong>, and <strong>S</strong>.</p>
      <div style="margin: 12px 0;">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="480" height="310" viewBox="0 0 480 310">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="480" height="310" fill="#fffde7" stroke="#ddd" stroke-width="1"/>
          <text x="95" y="32" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Glucose</text>
          <line x1="95" y1="40" x2="95" y2="68" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <polygon points="95,72 91,64 99,64" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="95" y="88" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Glyceraldehyde 3-Phosphate</text>
          <line x1="95" y1="96" x2="95" y2="148" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <polygon points="95,152 91,144 99,144" fill="#333"/>
          <path d="M 95 108 Q 145 112 145 126 Q 145 140 165 142" fill="none" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="168,142 160,138 160,146" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="172" y="110" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#222">NAD⁺</text>
          <text x="175" y="146" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#b71c1c">P</text>
          <text x="95" y="170" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">3-Phosphoglyceric acid</text>
          <line x1="95" y1="178" x2="95" y2="210" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <polygon points="95,214 91,206 99,206" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="95" y="232" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Phosphoenolpyruvic acid</text>
          <line x1="175" y1="228" x2="255" y2="178" stroke="#333" stroke-width="2"/>
          <polygon points="258,176 249,177 254,184" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="295" y="172" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Pyruvic acid</text>
          <line x1="295" y1="154" x2="295" y2="85" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <polygon points="295,80 291,88 299,88" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="295" y="70" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#1565c0" text-anchor="middle">R</text>
          <path d="M 295 132 Q 335 125 340 105" fill="none" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="341,101 336,108 344,109" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="348" y="102" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#222">NAD⁺</text>
          <text x="352" y="138" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#b71c1c">Q</text>
          <line x1="295" y1="182" x2="295" y2="255" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.8"/>
          <polygon points="295,260 291,252 299,252" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="295" y="278" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#2e7d32" text-anchor="middle">S + CO₂</text>
          <path d="M 295 205 Q 335 212 340 232" fill="none" stroke="#333" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <polygon points="341,236 336,229 344,228" fill="#333"/>
          <text x="352" y="206" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#b71c1c">Q</text>
          <text x="348" y="242" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#222">NAD⁺</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p>Select the correct combination for <strong>P</strong>, <strong>Q</strong>, <strong>R</strong>, and <strong>S</strong>.</p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The diagram shows glycolysis from glucose to pyruvic acid, followed by two anaerobic fermentation branches from pyruvic acid: one yielding <strong>R</strong> and the other yielding <strong>S</strong> + \(\text{CO}_2\).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Sign Conventions</strong><br/>Anaerobic conditions prevail, so pyruvic acid does not enter the Krebs' cycle.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>During glycolysis, oxidation of glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate (PGAL) reduces \(\text{NAD}^+\) to \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\). In both lactic acid fermentation and alcoholic fermentation, \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\) acts as the reducing agent and is reoxidised to \(\text{NAD}^+\).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>1. In the conversion of glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate to 3-phosphoglyceric acid (via 1,3-bisphosphoglycerate), \(\text{NAD}^+\) accepts two redox equivalents to form <strong>P</strong> = \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\).<br/>2. In both fermentation pathways from pyruvic acid, the reducing agent <strong>Q</strong> = \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\) is reoxidised to \(\text{NAD}^+\).<br/>3. The branch without \(\text{CO}_2\) release produces <strong>R</strong> = Lactic acid (catalysed by lactate dehydrogenase).<br/>4. The branch releasing \(\text{CO}_2\) produces <strong>S</strong> = Ethanol (catalysed by pyruvic acid decarboxylase and alcohol dehydrogenase).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Stoichiometry and redox balance are preserved because \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\) generated in glycolysis is reoxidised to \(\text{NAD}^+\) during fermentation. Therefore, <strong>P</strong> = \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\), <strong>Q</strong> = \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\), <strong>R</strong> = Lactic acid, and <strong>S</strong> = Ethanol.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
