  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_RESPIRATIONINPLANTS_DIAGRAM_Q03 - Steps and products of the citric acid cycle</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>Observe the simplified schematic of the Citric Acid Cycle (Krebs' cycle) below, where four key steps are labelled <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong>, <strong>C</strong>, and <strong>D</strong>.</p>
      <div style="margin: 12px 0;">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="480" height="320" viewBox="0 0 480 320">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="480" height="320" fill="#ffffff"/>
          <text x="240" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Acetyl CoA (2C)</text>
          <line x1="240" y1="32" x2="240" y2="62" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2.2"/>
          <path d="M 185 80 Q 240 62 295 80" fill="none" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2.2"/>
          <polygon points="298,81 289,75 292,83" fill="#c62828"/>
          <text x="145" y="88" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Oxaloacetic acid (4C)</text>
          <text x="335" y="88" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Citric acid (6C)</text>
          <path d="M 355 98 Q 390 130 375 162" fill="none" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2.2"/>
          <polygon points="373,166 373,157 381,161" fill="#c62828"/>
          <text x="405" y="135" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#1565c0">A</text>
          <text x="355" y="182" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">α-ketoglutaric acid (5C)</text>
          <path d="M 355 192 Q 335 245 275 268" fill="none" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2.2"/>
          <polygon points="271,270 278,263 280,271" fill="#c62828"/>
          <text x="352" y="242" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#1565c0">B</text>
          <text x="240" y="282" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Succinic acid (4C)</text>
          <path d="M 195 270 Q 130 245 120 192" fill="none" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2.2"/>
          <polygon points="119,188 116,197 124,195" fill="#c62828"/>
          <text x="122" y="242" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#1565c0">C</text>
          <text x="115" y="180" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#222" text-anchor="middle">Malic acid (4C)</text>
          <path d="M 110 162 Q 105 125 130 98" fill="none" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2.2"/>
          <polygon points="133,95 125,98 131,104" fill="#c62828"/>
          <text x="86" y="135" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#1565c0">D</text>
          <text x="240" y="175" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#555" text-anchor="middle">CITRIC ACID CYCLE</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <p>Which of the following correctly identifies the products formed at steps <strong>B</strong> and <strong>C</strong>?</p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Given Data and Conditions</strong><br/>The diagram shows the cyclic sequence of intermediates in the Citric Acid Cycle: Acetyl CoA (2C) + Oxaloacetic acid (4C) \(\rightarrow\) Citric acid (6C) \(\xrightarrow{\text{A}}\) \(\alpha\)-ketoglutaric acid (5C) \(\xrightarrow{\text{B}}\) Succinic acid (4C) \(\xrightarrow{\text{C}}\) Malic acid (4C) \(\xrightarrow{\text{D}}\) Oxaloacetic acid (4C).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Assumptions and Sign Conventions</strong><br/>One turn of the cycle oxidises one Acetyl CoA molecule in the mitochondrial matrix.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Relevant Formulae and Principles</strong><br/>During the TCA cycle, two decarboxylations occur (6C \(\rightarrow\) 5C and 5C \(\rightarrow\) 4C), three \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\) molecules are formed, one \(\text{FADH}_2\) is formed, and one substrate-level phosphorylation produces GTP.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>1. Step <strong>A</strong> (Citric acid 6C to \(\alpha\)-ketoglutaric acid 5C): involves decarboxylation (\(\text{CO}_2\) release) and reduction of \(\text{NAD}^+\) to \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\).<br/>2. Step <strong>B</strong> (\(\alpha\)-ketoglutaric acid 5C to Succinic acid 4C via succinyl-CoA): involves decarboxylation (\(\text{CO}_2\) release), reduction of \(\text{NAD}^+\) to \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\), and substrate-level phosphorylation converting GDP to GTP.<br/>3. Step <strong>C</strong> (Succinic acid 4C to Malic acid 4C): involves oxidation of succinate where \(\text{FAD}^+\) is reduced to \(\text{FADH}_2\).<br/>4. Step <strong>D</strong> (Malic acid 4C to Oxaloacetic acid 4C): involves reduction of \(\text{NAD}^+\) to \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 5: Check and Final Answer</strong><br/>Counting the carbon atoms confirms \(\text{CO}_2\) release at steps <strong>A</strong> (6C to 5C) and <strong>B</strong> (5C to 4C), and no carbon loss at <strong>C</strong> or <strong>D</strong>. Therefore, step <strong>B</strong> yields \(\text{CO}_2\), \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\), and \(\text{GTP}\), whereas step <strong>C</strong> yields \(\text{FADH}_2\).</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>B</strong>: \(\text{FADH}_2\) only; <strong>C</strong>: \(\text{GTP}\) and \(\text{CO}_2\)</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>B</strong>: \(\text{CO}_2\), \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\), and \(\text{GTP}\); <strong>C</strong>: \(\text{FADH}_2\)</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>B</strong>: \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\) and \(\text{FADH}_2\); <strong>C</strong>: \(\text{CO}_2\) and \(\text{GTP}\)</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>B</strong>: \(\text{CO}_2\) and \(\text{FADH}_2\); <strong>C</strong>: \(\text{NADH} + \text{H}^+\) and \(\text{GTP}\)</p>]]></text></answer>
