  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_RESPIRATIONINPLANTS_DIAGRAM_Q04 - Electron transport system carriers and complexes</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>The schematic diagram below represents the Electron Transport System (ETS) in the inner mitochondrial membrane, with four components masked as <strong>I</strong>, <strong>II</strong>, <strong>III</strong>, and <strong>IV</strong>.</p>
      <div style="margin: 12px 0;">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="490" height="290" viewBox="0 0 490 290">
          <rect x="0" y="0" width="490" height="290" fill="#ffffff"/>
          <text x="65" y="22" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#444" text-anchor="middle">Intermembrane space</text>
          <text x="235" y="22" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#444" text-anchor="middle">Inner Mitochondrial Membrane</text>
          <text x="415" y="22" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#444" text-anchor="middle">Matrix</text>
